        "country_code": "ua",
        "front_dist_km": null,
        "text": "ISW previously assessed that Russian forces reportedly suffered around 1,298 casualties per square kilometer they seized or infiltrated in June 2026 and, at that rate, Russian forces would lose 6,574,590 servicemembers in capturing the remaining 5,065.17 square kilometers of Donetsk Oblast.[6] Putin and other Russian military commanders heavily aggrandized the claimed seizure of Kostyantynivka on July 3 and 4.",
